is false for half the rows.\n\nBoth reviewer gates re-run against r7 returned `false`/exit 1.\n\n**Fix:** A5 rescoped to the two production iOS rows (probe pair handed to A18 as a declared contrast); A9 split into **A9a** (macOS Mac Development), **A9b** (iOS, deferred, not created at C1), **A9c** (Developer ID).\n\n## The class, not the two strings\n\nr6 closed this exact defect class for the cross-platform *summary* (rule S1) and left the *assertion list* — the other prose projection of the same rows — unchecked. That's why two assertions sat stale under a 1024-check validator.\n\nNew **rule S2** derives every scope-bearing assertion's scope **three ways** (class predicates over the rows, an explicit list, the row statuses) and requires all three to agree. It enforces a **partition** per entitlement key — `present ∪ absent = all rows`, `present ∩ absent = ∅` — which is precisely what A5 and A18 violated, plus coverage in both directions so a future assertion naming an entitlement key without registering its scope fails closed. All ten scope-bearing entitlement assertions and all three profile assertions registered, not just the two reported.\n\n## Third stale claim, unreported by any verdict\n\nRegistering A6's scope required its clauses to render in the rationale document — which still carried the **r4** contract, granting `macos.host` the Keychain group r5 removed under rule K2. The verdict-05 F1 defect one revision later and one file over; R33 couldn't see it because R33 renders `grantClause`s, not assertions. The table also had no rows at all for A17/A18. Recorded in `S2.staleClaimsFound`, fixed, gated.\n\nTwo defects in the *new* gates surfaced from their own negative mutations and were fixed rather than worked around: R35's mention scan raised `KeyError` on a deleted assertion instead of failing closed (silently suppressing four pre-existing `[A-set]` gates), and the first R27 banned phrase `every iOS bundle` would have blocked A14's legitimate absence claim — narrowed to the defective presence shape.\n\n## Gates — all exit 0\n\n| gate | result |\n| --- | --- |\n| `validate_matrix.py` (R1–R36) | 1331 checks |\n| `mutate.py` | 164/164 (34 new) |\n| `check-portal-consumer.py` | 44 checks / 2 consumers |\n| `preserve.py` r7→r8 | 94 assertions |\n| reviewer A5 + A9 gates | false/exit 1 → **true/exit 0** |\n| legacy guard, `task-board validate` | exit 0 |\n| `swift test` | 335 tests / 29 suites |\n\nNo entitlement decision, target row, profile row, record or C1 mutation set changed — the preservation harness proves the only top-level keys differing from r7 are `revision`, `supersedes`, `revisionLog`, `verification`. One board field touched: `TASK-260728-q5kjta.scope`, revision label r7→r8, **0-character delta**. No portal mutation, no product source or spec touched.","ttft_ms":4853,"ttft_stream_ms":4357,"time_to_request_ms":71,"type":"result","duration_ms":1367347,"uuid":"00e3af3e-7e1f-4c76-b88a-fa424ec1451d"}
